# Authentication scope (approved September 2026)

- Firebase Auth replaces Supabase Auth; MySQL and the Go API own users and permissions.
- Google is primary; email/password supports verification/reset. Never add phone authentication.
- Keep public browsing and `/register-as-brahmin/` accessible without login.
- Anonymous registration creates an unverified pending applicant profile, not a Firebase account.
- Verified Firebase email ownership permits an explicit profile claim; claiming never approves a Purohit.
- Booking submission requires an active account and server-verified email.
- Every active account has customer capability; provider approval/suspension is separate from whole-account status.
- Admin privileges are database controlled. Never derive them from signup intent or client fields.
- Preserve internal IDs and old relationships. Legacy account mappings require operator-reviewed evidence.
- Staging Firebase project is `brahminbooking-staging`; production is `brahminbooking`.
- Keep KRIPA service credentials separate. Never bundle Firebase Admin credentials in Pages.
- Deploy this phase to staging only; registration-form simplification and Panchang presentation are later priorities.
